  "result": "Perfect! All 176 tests pass. I've added comprehensive payment recording functionality:\n\n**New file `src/payments.js`:**\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice:\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to `invoice.payments` array\n   - Creates payments array if missing\n   - Updates invoice status:\n     - `'paid'` when total payments >= invoice total\n     - `'partially_paid'` while amount is still owed\n   - Error codes:\n     - `NOT_ISSUED` if invoice status is not 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID` if amount is not a positive integer (in cents)\n     - `OVERPAYMENT` if payment exceeds remaining balance\n   - Never mutates the original invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates amount still owed:\n   - Returns `total - sum(payments)` in cents\n   - Returns 0 for fully paid invoices (never negative)\n   - Works on any invoice (draft, issued, partially paid, paid)\n\n**Changes to `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `NOT_ISSUED`: \"Only issued or partially paid invoices can receive payments.\"\n- Added `OVERPAYMENT`: \"Payment exceeds the amount still owed.\"\n\n**Tests added (17 new, 176 total):**\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions: issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid\n- Rejecting payments on draft invoices\n- Validating amount (positive integer, no overpayment)\n- Balance calculations with various payment scenarios\n- Complex invoices with discounts, VAT, and tier discounts\n- Immutability verification\n\n**Key design:**\n- Payments are immutable once recorded\n- Status updates automatically based on payment coverage\n- All amounts in cents (integer cents only)\n- Multiple partial payments supported\n\nAll 176 tests pass. \u2705",
